{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20095",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 4.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Hi there, the chair's free, sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.21,
      "end_seconds": 12.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "Hi doctor, um, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.32,
      "end_seconds": 18.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, uh, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.76,
      "end_seconds": 24.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.3,
      "end_seconds": 30.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "He's been waking up breathless at night, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.32,
      "end_seconds": 35.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.35,
      "end_seconds": 56.37,
      "duration_seconds": 15.02,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, it's been going on for two months. I took the morning off to come in today. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.4,
      "end_seconds": 59.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "What eases it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.57,
      "end_seconds": 65.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "It, It settles a little with sitting up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.94,
      "end_seconds": 69.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.48,
      "end_seconds": 74.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Honestly, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.23,
      "end_seconds": 78.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.81,
      "end_seconds": 83.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I'd give it a six, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.93,
      "end_seconds": 87.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.58,
      "end_seconds": 100.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a tight stomach as well. The tight stomach? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.56,
      "end_seconds": 119.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Right, what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 119.98,
      "end_seconds": 130.98,
      "duration_seconds": 11.0,
      "text": "He takes carvedilol, 6.25 milligrams, twice a day. He takes metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.14,
      "end_seconds": 134.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.31,
      "end_seconds": 141.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.16,
      "end_seconds": 148.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "So, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.54,
      "end_seconds": 152.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure. Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.09,
      "end_seconds": 162.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure and diabetes are known to us, good to have that clear. Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.92,
      "end_seconds": 168.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.17,
      "end_seconds": 171.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.73,
      "end_seconds": 175.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.1,
      "end_seconds": 179.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.14,
      "end_seconds": 184.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.7,
      "end_seconds": 202.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.23,
      "end_seconds": 210.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "I was told I'm allergic to erythromycin, but I don't remember what reaction I had."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.4,
      "end_seconds": 216.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Did you get cough with blood, chest pain or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.79,
      "end_seconds": 224.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "No cough with blood, chest pain or fainting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.06,
      "end_seconds": 227.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Okay, how about palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.56,
      "end_seconds": 232.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I haven't had any palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.55,
      "end_seconds": 236.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.79,
      "end_seconds": 239.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.46,
      "end_seconds": 241.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.83,
      "end_seconds": 245.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Ah, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.07,
      "end_seconds": 249.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.5,
      "end_seconds": 257.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.69,
      "end_seconds": 286.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.9, blood pressure 131 over 83, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, heart rate 124."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.7,
      "end_seconds": 290.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.3,
      "end_seconds": 296.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Alright, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.36,
      "end_seconds": 332.18,
      "duration_seconds": 18.82,
      "text": "So, based on your history, it points towards fluid overload from heart failure. Let me just check I've got this right. You've been waking up breathless at night for two months, and no chest pain or cough with blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.94,
      "end_seconds": 337.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Ah, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.58,
      "end_seconds": 366.35,
      "duration_seconds": 26.77,
      "text": "We should do blood tests for fluid overload. We should do a chest X-ray for breathlessness. I'll start you on furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning, long term. You take it by mouth. It's for fluid retention. Weigh yourself every morning and tell us if you gain more than two kilos in three days. I'll also refer you to the community nursing team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.93,
      "end_seconds": 369.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.03,
      "end_seconds": 383.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "Let's hold off on a heart ultrasound for now, and if there's no change in two weeks we can revisit it. Let's plan a check in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.41,
      "end_seconds": 387.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.81,
      "end_seconds": 391.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.61,
      "end_seconds": 395.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 396.84,
      "end_seconds": 398.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}